{"id":"word:hebrew:H2934","type":"word","title":"טָמַן","subtitle":"H2934 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to hide (by covering over)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to טָמַן (H2934) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 31 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"טָמַן (ṭâman) means to hide (by covering over) First listed occurrence: 2Kgs 7 8."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"טָמַן","transliteration":"ṭâman","pronunciation":"taw-man'","strong":"H2934","lemmaId":"hebrew:H2934","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["טָ֘מַ֤ן","וַ/יַּטְמִ֑נוּ","וַ/יַּטְמִֽנוּ","טְמ֥וּנֵי","וַֽ/יִּטְמְנֵ֖/הוּ"],"morphs":[["HVqp3cp",6],["HVqsmsa",3],["HVqp3ms",3],["HC/Vhw3mp",2],["HR/Vqc",2],["HVqsmpc",1],["HC/Vqw3ms/Sp3ms",1],["HC/Vqw3ms",1],["HC/VNv2ms",1],["HC/Vqv2ms/Sp3ms",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"to hide (by covering over)","usage":"hide, lay privily, in secret.","full":"H2934. taman טָמַן verb hide, conceal , especially in earth (Late Hebrew id. ; whence perhaps Aramaic טְמֵן keep, preserve ; compare Arabic bury, hide (loan-word Frä 137 ); Aramaic , טְמַר id. ); — Qal Perfect טְמֵן Psa 35:8 2 t. etc; Imperfect וַיִּטְמֹן Gen 35:4 , etc.; Imperative suffix טָמְנֵהוּ Jer 13:4 ; טָמְנֵם Job 40:13 ; Infinitive construct לִטְמוֺן 31:33 ; Psa 64:6 ; Passive participle טָמוּן Job 3:16 3 t.; טְמוּנָה Josh 7:22 ; plural טְמֻנִים 7:21 ; construct טְמוּנֵי Deut 33:19 ; — 1 hide , with accusative Gen 35:4 (E), Exod 2:12 (E; dead body in sand), Josh 2:6 (J E; spies under flax-stalks), 7:21-22 , (J E; Achan's theft), Jer 13:4-5 , 6 , 7 (Jeremiah's girdle), 43:9-10 , (stones at Tahpanhes); hide, bury hand in dish ( צַלָּ֑חַת ) Prov 19:24 ; 26:15 (of עָצֵל the sluggard); טָמוּן נֵפֶל Job 3:16 hidden abortion , i.e. a lifeless child at once buried; חול טְמוּנֵי שְׂפֻנֵי Deut 33:19 (poem); of hiding iniquity עון Job 31:33 ; hiding the wicked in the dust עפר 40:13 . 2 often of hiding, concealing, secretly laying a snare רֶשֶׁת Psa 9:16 ; 35:8 , followed by לִי 31:5 ; רִשְׁתָּם שַׁחַת 35:7 ; מַּח followed by לִי 140:6 ; 142:4 ; followed by לרגלי Jer 18:22 ; חבל Job 18:10 ; מוֺקשׁים Psa 64:5 . 3 טָמוּן that which is darkened = darkness , Job 40:13 nearly = בט חֲבשׁ ׳פניהם ׃שְׁאוֺל bind their faces in darkness (i.e. the wicked); hide = reserve 20:26 all darkness is held in reserve for his treasures , i.e. all calamities are stored up for them. Niph`al Imperative י מַּחַד ׳מִמְּנֵי בֶּעָפָר חִטָּמֵן Isa 2:10 hide thyself in the dust, from before the terror of ׳י . Hiph`il (or Qal ? Ba ZMG 1889, 180 ) Imperfect וַיַּטְמִנוּ וַיֵּלִכוּ 2Kin 7:8 (twice in verse) and they went and hid (it), i.e. plunder from Aramaic camp.","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"2Kgs 7 8","keyReferences":["2Kgs 7 8","2Kgs 7 8","Deut 33 19","Exod 2 12","Gen 35 4","Isa 2 10","Jer 13 4","Jer 13 5"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":31,"occurrences":[{"reference":"2Kgs 7 8","book":"2Kgs","chapter":7,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יַּטְמִ֑נוּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vhw3mp"},{"reference":"2Kgs 7 8","book":"2Kgs","chapter":7,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יַּטְמִֽנוּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vhw3mp"},{"reference":"Deut 33 19","book":"Deut","chapter":33,"verse":19,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"טְמ֥וּנֵי","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqsmpc"},{"reference":"Exod 2 12","book":"Exod","chapter":2,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַֽ/יִּטְמְנֵ֖/הוּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3ms/Sp3ms"},{"reference":"Gen 35 4","book":"Gen","chapter":35,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּטְמֹ֤ן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3ms"},{"reference":"Isa 2 10","book":"Isa","chapter":2,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/הִטָּמֵ֖ן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/VNv2ms"},{"re